// Prologue: The Edge. Story bible section 7.0. Wren and Isolde at the Greyfold's edge at dusk.
// The tutorial is characterisation. Isolde speaks plainly (style guide section 6, the exception).
// Commands (<<flag>>, <<survey_hint>>, <<bind_prompt>>, <<tutorial>>) are implemented in PRG-08.

title: Prologue_Edge_Arrive
---
<<flag prologue.started 1>>
Isolde: Stop. Here is far enough.
Isolde: Tell me what you see, journeyman.
-> White. It's closer than last month.
    Isolde: Nine wingspans closer. I measured. #plant:4.6
-> The Half-Cathedral. Its bells are still up.
    Isolde: They ring, some nights. Nobody's inside to ring them. #plant:6.12
-> Nothing. I can't look straight at it.
    Isolde: No one can. That's the first thing to learn about the Blank. Look beside it.
Isolde: We'll take a page of it before dark. Then I'll show you something.
<<tutorial survey>>
Isolde: The lens. Slow. Let the pen find the line; don't push it.
<<jump Prologue_Edge_Survey>>
===

title: Prologue_Edge_Survey
---
<<if $vantage_inked == 1>>
    Isolde: There. Feel the page take it?
    Isolde: Now bind it. A page without a memory is only a drawing.
    <<bind_prompt isolde.first_sight>>
    Isolde: I'll give you mine. Write it exactly.
    Isolde: "A child at the edge of the white, looking straight at me. The only one who could."  #plant:5.3
    -> Me.
        Isolde: You. Six years old and not afraid of it. I was terrified.
    -> Why that memory?
        Isolde: Because it's the truest thing I own. Binding wants the truest thing.
    -> ...
        Isolde: Quiet suits a cartographer. Seal it.
    <<tutorial seal>>
    <<flag prologue.sealed_edge_page 1>>
    <<jump Prologue_Edge_Dusk>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Prologue_Edge_Dusk
---
Isolde: Good. That's the last thing I can teach you standing still.
<<tutorial strike>>
Isolde: Smudges come out at dusk here. Quill up. Strike where the ink is thickest.
// Three smudges; combat tutorial; Isolde fights beside Wren.
<<flag prologue.first_smudges 1>>
Isolde: You hold it like Voss taught you. Loosen your wrist. #plant:5.5
<<jump Prologue_Edge_Departure>>
===

title: Prologue_Edge_Departure
---
Isolde: Wren.
Isolde: I'm going in.
-> You don't have a tether.
    Isolde: No.
-> Then I'm coming.
    Isolde: You'll try. That's rather the point. #plant:5.2
-> Why?
    Isolde: Because I drew something I shouldn't have. And because someone in there is owed a visit. #plant:5.2
Isolde: Don't anchor what I've drawn. Come find why.
Isolde: Look at me. Only at me. Then look beside the white. #plant:5.3
<<flag prologue.isolde_entered 1>>
// Isolde walks in. Player follows. Clarity drains. Fade to paper.
===

title: Prologue_Shore_Wake
---
// Saltmarrow shore. Wren wakes. Sable stands over her.
Sable: Wings high, stranger. You've come a long way to be lost.
Sable: Guild cowl. No licence on you. No atlas either.
-> Where is this?
    Sable: The Saltmarrow. The far side of everything. The Blank spat you out here; it does that, sometimes.
-> How long was I gone?
    Sable: Long enough that the Guild's stopped looking. A fortnight, by the tide.
-> There was a kite. Isolde Marr.
    Sable: Nobody came out but you. Nobody ever comes out. #plant:5.2
Sable: Quay's up the boardwalk. Everything there has a price. Including me.
<<flag prologue.woke_on_shore 1>>
<<flag act1.started 1>>
===
